    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense for the street characters. To really drive home that \"world vs. world\" contrast we talked about, I want to make sure the distinction between the professional/intellectual side and the street side is crystal clear through their backgrounds too. \n\nSince the detective is meant to be the pillar of order and intellect, what kind of background/heritage would best suit him to keep that contrast sharp? And if we're looking at the higher-level corruption—not the street guys, but the white-collar criminals or the political figures who are secretly pulling the strings—what kind of profiles would you suggest for them to maintain that specific tension between the \"civilized\" world and the urban underworld?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
