      "content": "You might position your detective as a first-generation immigrant or upper-middle-class intellectual whose pristine, law-abiding persona serves as the moral anchor against the chaos below. For the white-collar villains, consider a trope like advanced age and rigid, sterile professions—such as a retired professor or a high-ranking judge—who wielded their crimes through obscure legal loopholes and bureaucratic malfeasance rather than thug tactics. This contrast emphasizes a terrifying shamelessness where crime is treated as a mundane, civilized exercise, not a brutal street struggle. It forces your protagonist to realize that the most dangerous monsters in the city don't always wear suits or spray paint; some simply manage the ledger. This duality highlights that order can rot from within just as easily as it breaks from the outside, deepening the tragedy of his isolation.",
